<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">7 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 7 December, from 43 BCE to 1975.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">43 BCE</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cicero is killed on Mark Antony's orders</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Proscribed by the Second Triumvirate, Marcus Tullius Cicero was overtaken by soldiers near Formiae and killed. His head and hands were displayed in the Forum, where he had attacked Antony in his Philippics.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-triumvirate">Second Triumvirate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1732</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Theatre Royal, Covent Garden, opens</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">John Rich opened his new theatre at Covent Garden with Congreve's The Way of the World. Twice rebuilt after fires, it became the Royal Opera House in 1892.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">Theatre</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1815</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Marshal Ney is executed by firing squad</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Michel Ney, whom Napoleon called 'the bravest of the brave', was shot in Paris for treason after joining his former emperor during the Hundred Days. He refused a blindfold and is said to have given the order to fire.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1941</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Japan attacks Pearl Harbor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Japanese carrier aircraft struck the US Pacific Fleet at Pearl Harbor, Hawaii, killing more than 2,400 Americans and sinking or damaging 19 ships. The United States entered the Second World War the next day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1975</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Indonesia invades East Timor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Indonesian forces invaded East Timor nine days after Fretilin declared independence from Portugal. The occupation cost an estimated 100,000 to 180,000 lives before a UN-supervised vote led to independence.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-timor">East Timor</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a></div></li></ol>
